{
  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports Outlook on laptop not receiving new mail since this morning; need account, mailbox usage, and devices per KB-009 quick checks."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0101",
  "reason": "Confirm laptop is online and check for warnings, per KB-009 quick check 3, for Outlook not syncing."
}

{
  "user_id": 1,
  "reason": "Check for failed or unusual sign-ins that could explain Outlook on laptop failing to sync since this morning."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for reporting this. I checked your account and your laptop: your mailbox has plenty of room, the laptop is online with no warnings, and there are no sign-in problems on your account. That points to the Outlook app on the laptop rather than your mailbox. Could you please do the following and let us know the results? 1) Open Outlook on the web (in a browser, signed in to your work account) and tell us whether the new messages appear there. 2) In Outlook on the laptop, go to the Send / Receive tab and make sure Work Offline is not turned on. 3) Close Outlook completely and reopen it. 4) If it still isn't updating, restart the laptop. If new mail still doesn't arrive after that, reply to this ticket and we will rebuild your Outlook profile or pass it to a senior technician.",
  "internal_note": "User is Dana Whitfield (user_id 1), CEO, VIP, active, not blocked, no failed logins. Mailbox 17.4% used (8.9 GB of 50 GB), so KB-010 does not apply. Laptop BL-LT-0101 is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:03 UTC, 60.5% disk free, no warnings. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days show only successful VPN and M365 sign-ins with Duo push, all in usual hours, no anomalies. Not yet done: KB-009 step 1 (user confirms whether Outlook on the web shows new mail). Next steps per KB-009: check Work Offline, restart Outlook and laptop, then rebuild the profile if needed. If OWA also lacks new mail, escalate per KB-009 (possible service issue or mailbox transport problem). Ticket is P3, but the requester is the CEO, so a quick follow-up is worthwhile.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
